<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">C.3 Experiment 3: Semantic Convergence</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We embedded all adjective-set completions from Experiment 3 using <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">text-embedding-3-large</span>,
standardized the vectors with <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">StandardScaler</span>, and reduced them to two dimensions
with UMAP (<span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_neighbors=35</span>, <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">min_dist=0.15</span>, <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">metric=cosine</span>, <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">random_state=3</span>).
Each trial produced a single embedding; similarity was measured using cosine distance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T16" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 16: </span>Pairwise cosine similarity distributions in the original embedding space (Experiment 3). Experimental adjective sets exhibit significantly higher within-condition similarity than any control.</figcaption>
